<title>BELGIUM: Monceau-Zolder 1996 net rises 32 pct.</title>
<headline>Monceau-Zolder 1996 net rises 32 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>12 months to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit	     1,016  vs  776</p>
<p>    Group net profit	    1,002  vs  757</p>
<p>    Gross dividend (francs)     147  vs  133</p>
<p>    Dividend income		 478  vs  406</p>
<p>    Capital gains		   972  vs  451</p>
<p>NOTE - Holding company Monceau-Zolder is the financial arm of the Brederode group with interests in insurance and telecommunications.</p>
<p>The company said that following the expiry on April 30 of 423,660 warrants giving rights to new, reduced withholding tax (VVPR) shares it would strip the shares, so that there tax advantage was traded separately.</p>
<p>The warrants can be exercised from April 1.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 771</p>
</text>
